title: InsureNext Partner Programs: C4 Container {near: top-center; shape: text; style.font-size: 24}
direction: down

underwriter: Underwriter {shape: person}
ops: Insurance Ops {shape: person}
ds: Data Scientist {shape: person}
partner: Partner system (partner backend) {style.stroke-dash: 4}

cognito: Amazon Cognito (partner client credentials, staff SSO federation)
extgw: Amazon API Gateway: external /v1 (WAF, usage plans, validation) {style.fill: "#e8f0fe"}
intgw: Amazon API Gateway: internal /internal/v1 {style.fill: "#e8f0fe"}

opsui: Ops interface (programs, questions, version history, approvals) {style.fill: "#e6f4ea"}

django: Django platform (system of record) {
  ext: External API (process group ext) {style.fill: "#e6f4ea"}
  int: Internal API (process group int) {style.fill: "#e6f4ea"}
  svc: Shared service layer (programs, questions, validation, config merge, payload preflight, rating orchestration, publish)
  uw: Underwriting UI (existing)
  ext -> svc
  int -> svc
  uw -> svc
}

pg: Postgres (additive schema) {shape: cylinder}
raters: "Rater Lambdas: one published version per rating_engine_version (existing, config-aware, inputs declared in code)"
ci: Rater repo CI (tests, manifest generation, compatibility check, backtest) {shape: page}
cw: CloudWatch (Logs, EMF metrics, Alarms, Dashboards) {shape: hexagon}
lake: S3 log lake + DB exports -> Athena {shape: stored_data}

partner -> cognito: get token
partner -> extgw: HTTPS + token
extgw -> django.ext
underwriter -> django.uw
ops -> opsui
opsui -> intgw: SSO token
intgw -> django.int
ds -> ci: pull requests
ds -> opsui: approve rating changes
ci -> raters: deploy published Lambda version
ci -> intgw: register rater version + manifest
ci -> intgw: read live programs (compatibility check)
lake -> ci: replay set (past rating_run inputs)

django.svc -> pg: SQL
django.svc -> raters: invoke (declared inputs + combined config)

extgw -> cw: access logs + metrics
intgw -> cw
django -> cw: JSON logs + EMF
raters -> cw: Powertools logs + EMF
cw -> lake: subscription -> Firehose
pg -> lake: daily export
